  "transmittance_not_entered": "The transmittance graphs are held so anyone can check a reading against the exact image, and NO value is entered from them. plan.md 5.3: a table a model builds by reading pixels off a rendered curve is an inference, E6, and may enter neither a card nor the store; a person reading the same graph is operator_read E3, to the precision the graph supports. This seat did read them by pixel on 2026-09-24, on the person's instruction to estimate the confocal power at other objectives, and entered nothing from it. The person was told and offered two routes: read the needed values themselves, or have architecture change the rule. Recorded for whoever takes it up: the pixel reading, scaled by the 20x transmittance, reproduced the measured 4x and 10x powers within 3 percent at all three lines.",
  "for_1064_nm": "The graphs stop at 1000 nm. The person proposed using the 1000 nm value for the 1064 nm trapping laser. plan.md 5.3 allows an endpoint to stand in for values beyond it only where the curve is flat at that end. By eye, the Lambda D curves are close to flat near 1000 nm; the 40xC WI curve is still falling steeply there -- and it is the one objective Nikon marks for laser trapping. So for the 40x the 1000 nm value is neither a bound nor an approximation at 1064 nm. Not entered either way, for the reason above.",
  "license_note": "Specification values and identifiers only; the graph images are Nikon's, held for verification."
}
